ne -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" story-wiki 2>&1 | tail -2; diff /tmp/outline7.md story-wiki/Outline.md"]], "output": "```console\n76c76\n<   - *rev 7, partial B-sensitivity (`background_reference_shift.csv`; German, ACS-Employment, up to 30 instances, German RF n=9–10):* the exact top-3 set of the B=50 reference stays the same under B=20 for 23–47%, under k-means-50 for 50–89%, under B=200 for 46–100% of instances. So the reference's top-3 depends on the background draw even at B=200 against B=50, and it moves toward stability with B but does not settle; this is *not yet* the floor-b-vs-B curve (that needs two independent draws at each B, same instances as floor a), so the paper still says \"at B=50\" and presents these as reference shifts, with n. **German MLP retraining floors are unusable** (AUC filter kept 1/24 bootstrap and 3/24 hyperparameter retrainings; only `c_seed` kept 6/15): the paper shows floor c for German MLP as not available, not as a number.\n---\n>   - *rev 7, partial B-sensitivity (superseded by rev 8 below for floor b) (`background_reference_shift.csv`; German, ACS-Employment, up to 30 instances, German RF n=9–10):* the exact top-3 set of the B=50 reference stays the same under B=20 for 23–47%, under k-means-50 for 50–89%, under B=200 for 46–100% of instances. So the reference's top-3 depends on the background draw even at B=200 against B=50, and it moves toward stability with B but does not settle; this is *not yet* the floor-b-vs-B curve (that needs two independent draws at each B, same instances as floor a), so the paper still says \"at B=50\" and presents these as reference shifts, with n. **German MLP retraining floors are unusable** (AUC filter kept 1/24 bootstrap and 3/24 hyperparameter retrainings; only `c_seed` kept 6/15): the paper shows floor c for German MLP as not available, not as a number.\n82c82\n< - **The abstract's order:** (1) at deployment budget a single run gives the right top-3 for ≥ 90% of instances in the non-trivial cells and fails only in near-tie instances; (2) below default it degrades by a mapped amount (guidance table); (3) the dominant instability is the background and the model, not the run; (4) scope. Wording of the verdict is \"conditional\": reliable for the attribution as defined, under stated budget and margin conditions; not a certificate against the definition's own sensitivity.\n---\n> - **The abstract's order (rev 8):** (1) at deployment budget a single shap run gives the right top-3 for ≥ 90% of instances in the d ≥ 16 cells (0.90–0.97 per model; 0.60–0.87 in the smallest-margin quartile Q1, 1.0 in Q2–Q4) and fails in near-tie instances; (2) below default it degrades by a mapped amount (guidance table); (3) at B=50 the exact explanation moves more with the background draw than the shap default moves between runs (floor b below floor a in 24 of 24 default-budget rows), a gap that shrinks as B grows and does not hold against paired Kernel SHAP at the same budget; (4) scope (d ≥ 16 two populations, one trained model each, B=50). Wording of the verdict is \"conditional\": reliable for the attribution as defined, under stated budget and margin conditions; not a certificate against the definition's own sensitivity.\n83a84,89\n> - **Rev 8 (from `analysis`'s answers on experiment-repo#5; files on `paper-repo` `dev` c4e1032).**\n>   - **Floor b by B (K=10 independent backgrounds, same instances as floor a; `floor_b_by_background.csv`):** median top-3 agreement B20 0.46, B50 0.62, B200 0.75, k-means-50 0.72. So the background-draw part shrinks with B, as idea-review expected, and a part of the reference's instability (the choice of reference distribution: k-means 0.72 < B200 is not a draw effect) remains. Against the shap default at the default budget floor b is below floor a in 24 of 24 rows (68 of 68 largest-sampled rows), but **against paired Kernel at the same budget the sign is mixed** (13 of 24 positive, 7 with CI above 0). The co-headline is therefore stated for *shap's default estimator at B=50*, with the B curve; \"the value function, not the run, dominates\" is not stated for paired Kernel SHAP or as\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "e98ff558-9b16-5475-847f-b668f8d8a9ec", "at": 1795644858.4479053, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 57434, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "0171cba7425985dc66c8c6a74b826b2e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "f23ddecc-4914-5c7d-a0ee-9f7aeca28e2c", "at": 1795644858.4506786, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 57435, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "0171cba7425985dc66c8c6a74b826b2e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "d76d9ba0-f2ed-5f18-adc0-55706603bc02", "at": 1795644858.453114, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 57436, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "0171cba7425985dc66c8c6a74b826b2e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "7406f4ba-ff73-5823-aa94-f75feb33f276", "at": 1795644858.5571482, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 57437, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "0171cba7425985dc66c8c6a74b826b2e", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credential-required", "repository": 